   ​[head=3]On Grayspeak[/head]

   Before beginning, having some understanding of the history of Grayspeak is important. Any language is the culmination of culture and history. Learning culture can help inform you of the logic behind the language.

   Grayspeak is what is called a “[bold]creole[/bold],” or in maybe more understandable terms, a contact language. Language is like a liquid; based on circumstances they can remain apart, but sometimes they mix together until you can't tell what's what!

   Grayspeak is much like that. As the gray societies of space came into contact with alien culture, they clinged to it and reveled in it and made it their own. A tasty beverage made from the mixing of two delicious histories!

   So this means that while communication between your average NanoTrasen employee and a gray can happen without friction, sometimes there are phrases that can be a little difficult to understand.

   ………………………………………………………………………………

   ​[head=3]On Communication[/head]

   Better than books, the best teacher for you will be communication with grays! You will quickly learn where your knowledge isn't enough. However, diving straight in can be intimidating.

   Communication is a dance. The exchanging of ideas and thoughts through words is something people take for granted until you find yourself in one of these situations. The worst thing you can do is suddenly stop. You're likely to bump into your dancing partner if you do!

   If there's something you or your partner don't understand, don't just leave it there. Single things out. Ask questions! To be a true language learner you need to be constantly moving back and forth with them. It can be hard for your partner if they don't know what you're having trouble with. Try asking things like “What does 'blin' mean?” or “Could you rephrase that?”

   Which is why the first words you'll learn are question words.

   Your communication partner will likely be asking things. Being able to single out questions will give you a leg up on being able to communicate and keep the dance going!

