   Thank you for reading the first chapter of Oum Erth! I hope you found it entertaining as you did formative. This is however just the first step in your long journey towards a better understanding and connection to your co-workers and potential friends!

   To peel back the curtain, you may have noticed some of those questions were difficult and using words that were not taught to you yet. This is not to discourage you, but to show you that sometimes full context is beyond us.

   By seeing it here without knowing what it means, you can make a guess. That is the heart of learning! The unknown before you requires you to guess. Then you learn if you're right or wrong. Mistakes are lessons of their own, and the building blocks upon which a master is made. It's important to hone your guessing skills. Plus, the more exposure you have to something before you learn it, the more likely it is to stick!

   So please look forward to the next chapter.

   Farewell!

   T.R.N.

