   ​[head=3]Culture Corner![/head]

   Comics, primarily webcomics, have long been popular amongst the myriad of gray societies. Before their meaning was fully comprehended, many scholars debated their meanings.

   Today, many grays make comics using ancient human webcomics as a basis. They span a vast span of genres and styles. We've included one of the most famous scenes from the gray comic “Life”

   It is an impactful science-fiction tragedy about genetic experiments to make grays capable of mammalian-like birth. It is about the folly of playing god and a reminder of what it means to be a gray.

   It holds many prestigious awards. The impact from this scene is noted for its lack of dialogue, images being a bridge between cultures! Please enjoy.

   (The comic depicts a gray rushing through some kind of medbay. They are seen talking to various staff members. The final panel has them entering a room where another gray is sitting in a hospital bed, sobbing. They are gripping their stomach tightly. The imagery is raw.)

